From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.xyz>
Subject: [PATCH] net: lwip: seed rand() and use random TCP initial
 sequence numbers

Nothing seeds rand() before lwip_init(), so lwIP picks the same first
local TCP and UDP port on every boot, and its default tcp_next_iss()
starts every connection at the same sequence number (6509 in QEMU, for
each connection). A board that reboots and loads the same files again
opens exactly the connections of its previous boot: same addresses,
same ports, same sequence numbers. A server that still holds those
connections (TIME_WAIT, or LAST_ACK when U-Boot never acknowledged the
server's FIN before booting) answers the new SYN as an old duplicate,
and the transfer fails with "HTTP client error 5". TFTP reuses its UDP
port the same way.

Seed rand() from the hardware RNG when there is one, mixed with the
timer, before lwip_init(), and define LWIP_HOOK_TCP_ISN to use rand().

Seen on the Raspberry Pi 400 network-booting over and over with serial
reboots: about one boot in five stopped at the prompt after every
HTTP and TFTP try had failed, while the Ethernet controller, the
driver and lwIP's link and IP layers counted no errors.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/lib/lwip/u-boot/lwipopts.h b/lib/lwip/u-boot/lwipopts.h
index 1c1adc5..1c34b28 100644
--- a/lib/lwip/u-boot/lwipopts.h
+++ b/lib/lwip/u-boot/lwipopts.h
@@ -179,6 +179,11 @@
 
 #define LWIP_STATS                      0
 
+/* A random initial sequence number per connection (default: a counter
+ * that starts at the same value on every boot) */
+#define LWIP_HOOK_TCP_ISN(local_ip, local_port, remote_ip, remote_port) \
+	((u32_t)rand())
+
 #define PPP_SUPPORT                     0
 
 #define LWIP_TCPIP_CORE_LOCKING		0
diff --git a/net/lwip/net-lwip.c b/net/lwip/net-lwip.c
index 8f8f9d6..5c286e6 100644
--- a/net/lwip/net-lwip.c
+++ b/net/lwip/net-lwip.c
@@ -20,6 +20,9 @@
 #include <lwip/timeouts.h>
 #include <net.h>
 #include <timer.h>
+#include <time.h>
+#include <rand.h>
+#include <rng.h>
 #include <u-boot/schedule.h>
 
 /* xx:xx:xx:xx:xx:xx\0 */
@@ -303,6 +306,26 @@ void net_lwip_remove_netif(struct netif *netif)
 	free(netif);
 }
 
+/*
+ * Seed rand() before lwIP picks its first local TCP and UDP ports and its
+ * TCP initial sequence numbers (LWIP_RAND, LWIP_HOOK_TCP_ISN). Without a
+ * seed every boot uses the same ports and sequence numbers, and a server
+ * that still holds the previous boot's connections (TIME_WAIT, LAST_ACK)
+ * takes the new SYNs for old duplicates. Use the hardware RNG when there is
+ * one, and mix in the timer either way.
+ */
+static void net_lwip_seed(void)
+{
+	struct udevice *dev;
+	u32 seed = 0;
+
+	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_DM_RNG) &&
+	    !uclass_get_device(UCLASS_RNG, 0, &dev))
+		dm_rng_read(dev, &seed, sizeof(seed));
+	seed ^= (u32)get_ticks() ^ (u32)timer_get_us();
+	srand(seed);
+}
+
 /*
  * Initialize the network buffers, an ethernet device, and the lwIP stack
  * (once).
@@ -313,6 +336,7 @@ int net_init(void)
 
 	if (!init_done) {
 		eth_init_rings();
+		net_lwip_seed();
 		lwip_init();
 		init_done = true;
 	}
-- 
